# Developer Experience (DX) Principles

## Primary Goal

A developer already using the Laravel AI SDK should be able to add agentic behavior with **one `use` statement and zero configuration changes**.

## Minimal Setup Example

```php
class SalesCoach implements Agent, Conversational
{
    use Promptable, RemembersConversations, ReActLoop;

    public function instructions(): string
    {
        return 'You are a sales coach...';
    }
}
```

## Fluent Usage

```php
// Simple
$result = (new SalesCoach)->forUser($user)->reactLoop('Hello!');

// With overrides and streaming callbacks
$result = (new SalesCoach)
    ->forUser($user)
    ->maxIterations(5)
    ->onAfterAction(fn ($tool, $args, $result, $i) => broadcast(...))
    ->onObservation(fn ($observation, $i) => logger()->info($observation))
    ->reactLoop('Analyze this transcript...');

$conversationId = $result->conversationId;
```

## DX Rules

1. **Zero config required** — sensible defaults, works out of the box
2. **Trait-based** — `use ReActLoop` is all you add to an existing agent
3. **Fluent API** — all configuration via chainable methods
4. **Familiar patterns** — follow Laravel AI SDK naming exactly
5. **Return AI SDK types** — `LoopResult` wraps `AgentResponse` transparently
6. **Callbacks are optional** — loops work perfectly with zero callbacks
7. **Progressive disclosure** — simple things are simple, complex things are possible
8. **Overridable internals** — `formatObservation()` and `loopShouldTerminate()` can be customized per-agent
